// Wildwood: an endless forest to walk through. This is its ground, sky and player: terrain
// without end, rolling forest floor with flat shelves, clearings, a network of trails, tall rock
// walls with scree at their feet and mountain ranges with snow on their peaks in the distance.
// Walk with WASD, F switches to flying and back; the panel of the forest library (H hides it)
// sets the season, the weather, the wind and the time of day.
//
// The forest library (forest/library) brings the state the sliders write, the materials, the
// weather, the sky and the HUD. This scene adds one file per concern in wildwood/: its constants
// and the fly toggle, the terrain materials, the terrain, the player and the view.
include ui/widgets
include trees/textures
include forest/library
include wildwood/state
include wildwood/materials
include wildwood/terrain
include wildwood/player
include wildwood/view

using box.view

$ {
  box.app.FpsTarget: {60}
  Scene: {
    reflections: true,
    environment: true,
    aerial_perspective: true,
    cookies: true,
    alpha_cutout: true,
    blend_modes: true,
    texture_blend: true,
    texture_layers: true,
    triplanar: true,
    diffuse_transmission: true,
    wind: true
  }
}
